  "raw": {
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001207840506": {
      "title": "Electrician",
      "description": "Electrician. Position Summary Under general supervision for routine, scheduled tasks and direct supervision for more complex tasks, inspects, maintains, tests, repairs, installs, and modifies electrical systems and all related equipment, fixtures, wiring, and appliances at the University. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Services a variety of electrical systems and equipment including lighting, alarm, signal, control, and power circuits. Examines and tests distribution panels, controls, circuits, fixtures, and motors to locate malfunctions such as blown fuses, short circuits, broken wires, loose connections, and worn motor brushes. Repairs electrical circuits and equipment by replacing faulty switches, sockets, plugs, fuses, insulators, and other components in the electrical system. Performs preventative maintenance on motors, generators, circuits, and other electrical equipment as scheduled. Assists employees and contractors in the installation of machinery and equipment. Fabricates and installs specialized electrical devices and modifies electrical systems as required. Measures, cuts, bends, threads, assembles, and installs electrical conduit using hand and power tools. Reviews blueprints, construction documents, and diagrams to assist in the planning of modifications or repairs to the electrical and related systems. Maintains the electrical safety program, tests, and inspections. Plans, estimates/quotes, and acquires materials and supplies for jobs. Coordinates work with employees in other classifications. Periodically assists in orienting, training, assigning, and checking the work of employees in lower classifications. Performs corrective maintenance, inspections, preventative maintenance, surveys, tasks, and tests of assigned areas, buildings, equipment, machinery, spaces, and systems. Reports findings, discrepancies, deficiencies, and necessary corrective action to management. Maintains the proper condition and appearance of areas, buildings, equipment, machinery, spaces, systems, and tools as assigned or directed by management. Documents activities, events, and occurrences with work orders, reports, schedules, logs, and journals as directed by management. Applies knowledge of general methods, procedures, safety, and techniques of the applicable trade. Applies and develops skills in methods, procedures, safety, techniques, equipment use, and tool use of the applicable trade. Maintains inventory of all related equipment, hardware, and supplies. Records data for service history, purchasing, and inventory. Cleans and leaves area of work in same condition or cleaner than prior to beginning of work. Performs all other duties as assigned by management. Requirements Minimum Qualifications A high school diploma or GED. Possession of a valid Electrical Journeyman License from the State of Michigan. Preferred Qualifications Aerial Lift Certification Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Advanced knowledge of the principles and practices of the electrical trade. Ability to read and understand blueprints and construction documents. Ability to train other employees on the electrical trade. Ability to follow, read, and understand, directions, drawings, instructions, manuals, policies, procedures, and schematics. Proficient in using a computer or mobile device to document activities, attendance, events, and occurrences. Knowledge and experience in utilizing tools and equipment safety. Physical Requirements Job requires repetitively lifting objects such as equipment, fixtures, materials, supplies, and tools under fifty (50) pounds with frequent bending and stooping and occasionally lifting objects over fifty (50) pounds. Job requires ascending/descending ladders, scaffolds, and stairs, using equipment or machinery, and traversing over or under obstacles all without restriction. Work Environment Working conditions vary whether indoors or outdoors, and an employee may be exposed to all weather conditions, high levels of heat and noise, confined spaces, dirt, dust, and smells. Licenses/Certifications Possession of a valid Electrical Journeyman License from the State of Michigan. Possession of a valid Driver’s License from the State of Michigan. Salary/Pay Information $39.27 per hour Anticipated Schedule Monday thru Friday, 7:30 Am to 3:30 Pm"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001228791206": {
      "title": "Dispensary Assistant",
      "description": "Dispensary Assistant. Position Classification FT Temporary Position Summary To provide service to students, faculty and staff members in all matters relative to instruments, equipment and materials used to provide patient care. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Distribute sterilized instruments and equipment and necessary materials and supplies to students, staff members and faculty utilizing the computerized tracking system. Receive instruments and materials from providers utilizing the computerized tracking system. Inspect cassettes to ensure all items are present, replace as necessary. Prepare, sterilize, and stock cassettes ready for distribution. Maintain and sterilize handpieces and other equipment. Assist in stocking all materials and supplies and preparing procedure kits for distribution. Assist in accepting and packaging lab cases utilizing the computerized tracking system. Performing other duties as requested, at any location Minimum Qualifications Education – A high school diploma or GED Employment - Six months to two years (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Physical Requirements Job requires repetitively lifting light weight objects where frequent bending or stooping alternates with lighter activities. Work Environment Occasional exposure to objectionable conditions or variations such as those found in variable weather conditions or light industrial settings. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Monday to Friday 8.30 AM to 5.00 PM"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001222987606": {
      "title": "Professor of Practice Doctor of Medical Science",
      "description": "Professor of Practice Doctor of Medical Science. Position Classification FT UDMPU 12 Month Faculty Position Summary The University of Detroit Mercy College of Health Professions, School of Health & Rehabilitation Sciences, is accepting applications for a full-time Principal Faculty appointment supporting the Doctor of Medical Science (DMS) Program. Rank is determined based on the candidate’s qualifications and experience. This faculty member will teach across the DMS and PA curricula, advise students, contribute to curriculum development and student assessment, participate in program evaluation and accreditation activities, and engage in service to the program, School, College, and University. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teach graduate-level courses in the DMS and PA Programs based on program needs and the faculty member's academic and clinical expertise. Teaching assignments may include in-person, hybrid, and online formats. Develop, revise, and coordinate courses, syllabi, learning objectives, instructional materials, learning activities, and assessments in collaboration with program faculty and leadership. Advise students. Monitor academic progress, identify concerns early, document advising as required, and connect students with appropriate academic or University resources. Mentor doctoral scholarly capstone projects and other culminating experiences as assigned by the DMS Program. Participate in the program’s assessment, outcomes evaluation, self-studies, and continuous improvement. Participate in student recruitment, admissions, orientation, progression, academic support processes, and graduation activities as assigned and consistent with University and program policies. Maintain appropriate student and academic records and comply with University policies regarding confidentiality, academic integrity, accessibility, and student information. Provide service through participation on program, School, College, and University committees and through appropriate professional and community activities. Support the mission and values of Detroit Mercy and contribute to an inclusive, respectful, student-centered learning environment. Perform other faculty duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Earned doctoral degree from an accredited institution. Examples may include PhD, EdD, DMS/DMSc, DHSc, or another relevant doctoral degree. A minimum of five years of clinical practice or health professions experience. A minimum of three years of teaching experience at an accredited institution of higher education, with experience appropriate to the instructional responsibilities of the position Ability to teach and engage students in a virtual learning environment Strong written, verbal, interpersonal, and organizational skills. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated experience designing, delivering, and evaluating graduate-level courses in online and hybrid learning environments. Demonstrated experience in curriculum development, course coordination, student learning assessment, program evaluation, and continuous quality improvement within higher education. Demonstratedexperiencewithaccreditationprocessesandstandardsinhealthprofessionseducation . Demonstratedexperienceadvisinggraduatestudentsanddoctorallearners,includingsupervisionofscholarlyprojects,capstoneexperiences,theses,dissertations,andstudent Evidence of effective interdisciplinary collaboration. Demonstrated commitment to preparing health professionals to serve diverse and underserved communities. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule This is a full-time, 12-month faculty appointment. The anticipated schedule is determined by program needs and assigned responsibilities. Duties may include on-campus and online teaching, meetings, student advising, scholarly or professional activity, and participation in program events. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY STATEMENT University of Detroit Mercy is an Equal Opportunity Affirmative Action Employer with a diverse faculty and student body and welcomes persons of all backgrounds."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001226931306": {
      "title": "Enterprise Systems Analyst",
      "description": "Enterprise Systems Analyst. Position Classification FT Admin Position Summary The Enterprise Systems Analystis responsible for the analysis, development, programming, testing, and maintenance of software and interfaces that enhance the University’s Ellucian Banner ERP system and third-party solutions. The overall support for the ERP includes assessing complex issues, creating and maintaining reports, evaluating business processes and rules, and providing technical assistance to the user community. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Define business requirements and develop business solutions; consult with the user community and external entities to define business requirements; create and document technical strategies to support the development of solutions in support of the University’s enterprise system. Data management and reporting through the development of data sets and report on University data. Create and maintain Oracle procedures and packages, as well as job scheduling. Gather requirements and create/maintain crosswalks to bridge data from other sources to current reporting systems. Develop user-friendly report dashboards. Ensure data integrity; diagnose system and data issues. Provide functional and technical support for the Banner ERP system and third-party applications. Perform other duties as assigned or requested. Minimum Qualifications Education – A college degree or four to eight years of work experience in a related field. Employment - Two years to five years (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Preferred Qualifications Ability to work in a fast-paced environment with changing priorities amongst a collaborative team. Prior professional IT experience in a Higher Education environment. Goal-oriented with strong initiative, imagination, and organizational qualities. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Experience with Ellucian Banner software, report-writing tools, and other database solutions. Excellent verbal and written communication skills including customer service and an ability to express oneself in an open, honest, and professional manner. Minimum of three years related experience; relational databases, advanced SQL programming skills, and business intelligence tools; experience with Banner, Oracle procedures and packages, Argos, and ISE Enterprise SCHEDULE preferred. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite with the ability to learn and apply new software and strive to consistently achieve excellence in all tasks and goals. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information $65K to $75K Annually Anticipated Schedule Position is primarily on the McNichols campus with partial work-from-home opportunities. Work schedule: Monday – Friday 8:30 AM – 5:00 PM"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001226921506": {
      "title": "Information Security Engineer",
      "description": "Information Security Engineer. Position Classification FT Admin Position Summary The Information Security Engineer is responsible for safeguarding the university’s computer systems, networks, and sensitive data from potential threats and vulnerabilities, such as malware, phishing attacks, unauthorized access, and misconfigurations. This role involves monitoring systems, identifying risks, implementing protective measures, and responding to security incidents to ensure the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of information. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Monitoring and Analysis: Monitor networks and systems for suspicious activities, anomalies, and potential security breaches. Analyze security logs and reports from various tools such as firewalls, intrusion detection/prevention systems (IDS/IPS), and security information and event management (SIEM) platforms. Incident Response: Investigate security alerts, determine root causes, and recommend corrective actions. Respond to security incidents by containing, eradicating, and recovering from threats. Risk Assessment: Perform vulnerability assessments and penetration testing to identify and mitigate risks. Collaborate with IT teams to address security vulnerabilities in hardware, software, and configurations. Policy and Compliance: Ensure compliance with industry standards, regulations, and internal security policies (e.g., FERPA, HIPAA, ISO 27001, GDPR) by utilizing tools such as compliance management platforms, automated auditing software, and adherence checklists. Assist in developing, implementing, and updating security policies and procedures. Security Tools and Technologies: Configure, maintain, and optimize security tools, such as antivirus/EDR, encryption tools, and firewalls. Stay current on emerging security technologies by obtaining certifications, participating in training sessions, attending industry events, and engaging in continuous learning. Recommend improvements to enhance the organization’s security posture. Documentation and Reporting: Create detailed reports on security incidents, including findings, actions taken, and future recommendations. Maintain documentation of security configurations, processes, and risk assessments. Minimum Qualifications Education – A college degree or four to eight years of work experience in a related field. Employment - Two years to five years (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Information Technology, or a related field (or equivalent experience). 3-5 years of experience in information security or a related IT role. Hands-on experience with firewalls, IDS/IPS, SIEMs, and endpoint protection tools. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong collaboration and communication skills to work effectively across teams and with stakeholders. Ability to explain technical security concepts to non-technical audiences. Attention to detail and the ability to multitask in a dynamic environment. Strong understanding of network protocols, operating systems, and cybersecurity tools. Analytical and problem-solving skills to identify and mitigate risks. Familiarity with scripting languages (e.g., Python, PowerShell) is a plus. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information $65K to $75K Annually Anticipated Schedule Monday to Friday 8.30 AM to 5.00 PM. Full-time, on-site with opportunities to work from home per policy. May require after-hours support for critical security incidents."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001225055106": {
      "title": "Registrar Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "Registrar Operations Coordinator. Position Classification FT Admin hourly Position Summary Provide broad, cross-functional operational support to the Office of the Registrar. This position works across all functional areas of the office, including the Transfer Team, Registration, and Records, to document and standardize office procedures, analyze operational and enrollment data, identify opportunities for efficiency, and support the Associate Vice President and University Registrar on special projects. Unlike positions assigned to a single functional area, this role is designed to move where support is most needed, giving the office added flexibility and a consistent point of contact for process documentation, data review, and project coordination. Essential Duties and Responsibilities List of essential functions with estimated percentage of time: Assist the Transfer Team with processing transfer credit, supporting the degree audit tool, and providing coverage during peak enrollment and evaluation periods. Create, maintain, and regularly update the Office of the Registrar's procedures manual, documenting standard operating procedures for registration, records, transfer, and front counter functions. Provide backup support at the front counter and with general customer service and data entry duties as needed. Collect, review, and analyze operational, enrollment, and student records data; prepare reports and recommendations for the Registrar and Associate Registrar to support decision-making. Support the Registrar on special projects, including system upgrades or implementations, policy and procedure reviews, and cross-departmental initiatives. Identify office-wide process improvement opportunities, research best practices at peer institutions, and recommend changes to workflows, forms, and communications; recommendations are reviewed and approved by the Registrar or Associate Registrar prior to implementation. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Education – A college degree or four to eight years of work experience in a related field. Employment - Two years to five years (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Preferred Qualifications Prior experience in a registrar's office, enrollment services, or other higher education administrative setting is preferred. Experience with process improvement, project coordination, or technical writing/documentation is a plus. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to write and organize clear procedural documentation. Proficiency in Microsoft Excel and other data and reporting tools, with the ability to analyze operational data and summarize findings for non-technical audiences. Familiarity with student information systems (e.g., Banner, Colleague, or Workday Student) and degree audit software preferred. Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple, competing priorities across different functional teams. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively, building effective working relationships across the office. Discretion in handling confidential student records and FERPA-protected information. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience. Anticipated Schedule Monday to Friday 8.30 Am to 5.00 PM. Some weekend or alternate hours may be required."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001224516606": {
      "title": "Director Disability Support Services",
      "description": "Director Disability Support Services. Position Classification FT Admin Position Summary Reporting to the Executive Director of Equal Opportunity, the Director of Disability Support Services will manage departmental operations, serve as the primary point of contact for academic, housing, and dining accommodations for students with disabilities, and manage department personnel. This role is specifically responsible for managing the accommodation process, assessing student needs, developing individualized academic support plans, coordinating accommodations with faculty and other units, and providing continuous support to ensure access to University programs and activities. The Disability Support Specialist will also serve as a liaison between students, faculty, and campus services, facilitating a supportive and inclusive learning environment. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Accommodation Case Management: Determine appropriate accommodations for individual students using an interactive process. Review, evaluate, and interpret relevant documentation and information to determine eligibility for reasonable accommodations, conferring with others as needed. Send timely, accurate, and appropriate written communication to confirm accommodations and outline next steps for implementation. Provide ongoing support, advising, and referrals to students with disabilities to ensure accommodations are appropriate and accurately communicated and implemented. Maintain records related to student accommodations, including documentation, case notes, and communications, using an electronic case management system. Communication, Outreach, and Education: Communicate relevant and timely information related to accommodations requests, renewals, and notifications to students, faculty, and other units. Serve as point of contact for faculty, departments, programs, and units seeking advice on the implementation of approved accommodations and provide guidance on access, confidentiality, and universal design. Provide information about disability services and the accommodations process to prospective and current students as well as departments, programs, and units. Develop outreach, communication, and training for students to support access and belonging. Operations (20%): Use and manage case management software (Accommodate) for student intake, accommodation tracking, and data reporting. Identify and manage vendors (e.g., interpreters, alternative format software, accessible technology). Maintain departmental supplies and accessibility-related purchases. Manage professional and student staff. Service and Other Activities : At the direction of Executive Director, works collaboratively with other employees across units to advance departmental and institutional priorities. Serve on related University committees and teams and contribute to relevant University and community activities. Perform additional responsibilities as assigned, including participating in professional development. Minimum Qualifications Education – A college degree Employment - Two to five years (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Proficient in word processing, spreadsheet, and database applications. Knowledge of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and Section 504 in the context of university settings. Ability to maintain current knowledge of best practices in the field of disability services and higher education. Ability to multitask and work cooperatively across units and with diverse populations. Strong written and verbal communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to interact effectively with students, faculty, and staff. Capacity to handle sensitive information with discretion and maintain confidentiality. Adherence to ethical standards and legal regulations related to disability services and accommodations. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Monday to Friday 8.30 AM to 5.00 PM"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001223842606": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor-Chemistry/Physics",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor-Chemistry/Physics. Position Classification PT Adjunct Faculty Position Summary The University of Detroit Mercy College of Engineering and Science invites applications for multiple part-time adjunct instructor positions in Physics. The successful candidate will be an effective and enthusiastic teacher at the undergraduate level with commitment to supporting a diverse population of undergraduate students. Primary Department needs are in both lecture and laboratory courses. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Deliver required course material in pedagogically sound manner, providing engaging strategies to support student success. Implement effective teaching strategies to create an inclusive, respectful, supportive, and welcoming learning environment for all students. Provide students a course syllabus consistent with University and Department guidelines that provides clear expectations to students, particularly regarding grading and course policies. Be available to provide support and assistance to students outside of class by holding office hours. Grade and return written work to students in a timely manner. Maintain appropriate records of students’ assessments. Submit mid-term and final grades by the scheduled deadlines. Other Responsibilities Review and adhere to University/College policies and guidelines with Asst. Dean and Chair. Notify the Asst. Dean and Chair as soon as possible if by an unavoidable circumstance you are unable to meet scheduled class sessions. Bring any incidents of Academic Integrity to the attention of the Asst. Dean. Refer at-risk students to Asst. Dean and appropriate University support services. Other duties, as assigned. Requirements Minimum Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: A minimum of a master’s degree in a relevant discipline is required. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule TBD Special Instructions to Applicants: Materials should include a curriculum vitae or resume, a one-page statement of personal teaching philosophy and experience. Review of applications begins immediately and continues as needed. Additional Information: The small classes and close collegial relationships make teaching in Detroit Mercy’s College of Engineering and Sciences both exciting and rewarding. The faculty forms a vibrant community of teaching scholars with a strong focus on professional and academic mentorship of students both formally and informally, both in class and out of class. The US News and World Report ranked Detroit Mercy in the top tier in the Midwest and first in Michigan in the category of Masters Comprehensive Universities. Michigan’s largest, most comprehensive private University, University of Detroit Mercy is an independent Catholic institution of higher education sponsored by the Sisters of Mercy and Society of Jesus. Detroit Mercy seeks qualified candidates who will contribute to the University’s mission, diversity, and excellence of its academic community. University of Detroit Mercy is an Equal Opportunity Affirmative Action Employer with a diverse student body and welcomes persons of all backgrounds."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001223844606": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor - Electrical & Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Adjunct Professor - Electrical & Computer Engineering. Employee Classification PT Adjunct Faculty Salary/Pay Information Pay Determined by the Number of Classes Position Summary University of Detroit Mercy is looking for highly qualified instructors with background in Electrical Engineering and specific Math courses such as Probability and Statistics to teach undergraduate courses in China in support of it’s programs with different Chinese universities. The teaching assignments are usually for 2-3 weeks and occasionally for 8 weeks. Essential Duties and Responsibilities (1) Teach assigned courses in China. (2) Coordinate with Chinese instructors during teaching. (3) Assign work and perform student assessment. (4) Cooperate with UDM leaders to help run the China program. (5) All other duties as assigned. Special Instructions to Applicants Please apply with a current CV and a list of courses that are qualified and/or experienced teaching. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001223847506": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor-Biology",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor-Biology. Employee Classification PT Adjunct Faculty Position Summary The University of Detroit Mercy College of Engineering and Science invites applications for multiple part-time adjunct instructor positions in Mathematics, Chemistry, Biology or Technical Writing. The successful candidate will be an effective and enthusiastic teacher at the undergraduate level with commitment to supporting a diverse population of undergraduate students. Essential Duties and Responsibilities (1) Implement effective teaching strategies that foster active student learning while creating an inclusive, respectful, supportive, and welcoming learning environment for all students. (2) Be committed to engaging a variety of strategies to support student success. Be available to provide support and assistance to students outside of class. Treat each student respectfully and supportively. (3) Provide students a course syllabus consistent with University and Department guidelines that provides clear expectations to students, particularly regarding grading and course policies. (4) Review University/College policies and guideline with Asst. Dean and Chair and adhere to these. (5) Bring any incidents of Academic Integrity to the attention of the Asst. Dean. (6) Grade and return written work to students in a timely manner. Maintain appropriate records of students’ assessments. Submit mid-term and final grades by the scheduled deadlines. (7) Refer at-risk students to Asst. Dean and appropriate University support services. (8) Notify the Asst. Dean and Chair as soon as possible if by an unavoidable circumstance you are unable to meet scheduled class session. (9) All other duties as assigned. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications A minimum of a master’s degree in a relevant discipline is required. Special Instructions to Applicants Materials should include a curriculum vitae or resume, a one page statement of personal teaching philosophy and experience. Review of applications begins immediately and continues as needed. Additional Information The small classes and close collegial relationships make teaching in Detroit Mercy’s College of Engineering and Sciences both exciting and rewarding. The faculty forms a vibrant community of teaching scholars with a strong focus on professional and academic mentorship of students both formally and informally, both in class and out of class. The US News and World Report ranked Detroit Mercy in the top tier in the Midwest and first in Michigan in the category of Masters Comprehensive Universities."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001222996306": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Mathematics",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Mathematics. Employee Classification PT Adjunct Faculty (in-person) Position Summary The University of Detroit Mercy College of Engineering & Science invites applications for multiple part-time adjunct instructor positions in Mathematics. Courses may include College Algebra, Pre-Calculus, Calculus 1, Calculus 2. The successful candidate will be an effective and enthusiastic teacher at the undergraduate level with commitment to supporting a diverse population of undergraduate students. Essential Duties and Responsibilities (1) Implement effective evidence-based teaching strategies that foster active student learning while creating an inclusive, equitable, respectful, supportive, and welcoming learning environment for all students. (2) Be committed to engaging a variety of strategies to support student success. Be available to provide support and assistance to students outside of class. Treat each student respectfully and supportively. (3) Provide students a course syllabus consistent with University and Department guidelines that provides clear expectations to students, particularly regarding grading and course policies. (4) Review University/College policies and guideline with Asst. Dean and Chair and adhere to these. (5) Bring any incidents of Academic Integrity to the attention of the Asst. Dean. (6) Grade and return written work to students in a timely manner. Maintain appropriate records of students’ assessments. Submit mid-term and final grades by the scheduled deadlines. (7) Refer at-risk students to Asst. Dean and appropriate University support services. (8) Notify the Asst. Dean and Chair as soon as possible if by an unavoidable circumstance you are unable to meet scheduled class session. (9) All other duties as assigned. Requirements Minimum Qualifications A minimum of a master’s degree in a relevant discipline is required. Preferred Qualifications Experience in the scholarship of Mathematics Education. Special Instructions to Applicants Materials should include a curriculum vitae or resume, a one-page statement of vision and strategies for supporting diverse student learning in mathematics. Review of applications begins immediately and continues as needed. Additional Information The small classes and close collegial relationships make teaching in Detroit Mercy’s College of Engineering and Sciences both exciting and rewarding. The faculty forms a vibrant community of teaching scholars with a strong focus on professional and academic mentorship of students both formally and informally, both in class and out of class. The US News and World Report ranked Detroit Mercy in the top tier in the Midwest and first in Michigan in the category of Masters Comprehensive Universities."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001221737806": {
      "title": "Campus Security Officer",
      "description": "Campus Security Officer. Position Classification FT Staff Position Summary To provide security services to the university; patrol campus and check resident halls and other buildings; maintain safe parking conditions on campus. Enforce University Parking rules and regulations, and enforce all University rules, regulations, policies, and procedures. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Patrols campus, providing security to all individuals on university property; checks and maintains security to all buildings and grounds. Provides security services (unlocking cars, starting stalled vehicles, emergency weather notification, unlocking/locking doors to buildings, etc.) Monitors facilities and reports any problems to Facilities Management for repair. Investigates university criminal/traffic complaints/concerns. Deals with parking concerns and enforcement. Performs other job related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Education -A high school diploma or GED Preferred Qualifications Courtesy, tact, and diplomacy are essential elements of the job. Work involves much personal contact with others inside and/or outside the university for purposes of giving or obtaining information, building relationships, or soliciting cooperation. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities A professional, patient demeanor that promotes a positive impression with co-workers and the University Community. Must have strong organizational and administrative skills, a good work ethic, and a positive attitude for interacting with other people. Strong communication skills, verbal and written. Computer proficiency in MS Word/Excel/Access is required, with a strong computer aptitude for learning various computer applications; Must be adaptable with the ability to accept and support change, highly skilled at multi-tasking and detail-oriented, able to effectively work independently or in a team environment, and able to work well under pressure. Demonstrate a professional demeanor and a clean, well-groomed appearance that creates a positive impression with customers and coworkers. Must be dependable, reliable, and confident working in a professional. Physical Requirements Job requires repetitive lifting of light-weight objects with frequent bending and stooping, or repetitively lifting average-weight objects where frequent bending or stooping alternates with lighter activities. Occasionally lifts heavy objects (over 50 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to unfavorable conditions such as weather conditions, or confined, noisy, or dirty locations. Licenses/Certifications Valid driver's license in good standing. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule TBD"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001219145506": {
      "title": "Personal Counselor",
      "description": "Personal Counselor. Position Classification FT Administrator Position Summary Personal Counseling attempts to strengthen students' self-esteem, to attain a deepened awareness of their potentials and limitations, and to make use of their intellectual and personal resources, enabling them to reach their full potential as integrated persons consistent with the university's mission. Student Wellness is a holistic presentation of services, resources, and skills to allow students to maximize their student experience, while maintaining balance, growth, and development as individuals. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide daily individual ongoing psychotherapy treatment. Engage in the process of triage, clinical assessment of need, and developing community referral sources as needed. Offer consultation services to faculty and staff when needed. Maintain and offer mental health referral sources when the need arises; develop appropriate printed and web-based mental health resource materials for students. Attend professional development conferences. Create and run student-based psychoeducational and therapy groups as needed, Design, implement, and present psycho-educational programming on a broad range of psychological issues including training for student leaders, PTV, SOAR, and other student-related events. 5% Assist in annual assessment and evaluation of student satisfaction data, Wellness Expo, and any outreach efforts. Attend professional development conferences. Attend and participate in division meetings as necessary. Design, implement, and present psycho-educational programming on a broad range of psychological issues. Act as liaison to particular university departments, offering knowledge and support regarding psychological and emotional aspects of student experience. Attend and participate in supervision sessions once per month. Maintain effective and accurate record-keeping, creating and maintaining charts in a timely manner. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Education – A college degree and a professional certificate or graduate degree. Employment - Two years to five years (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Preferred Qualifications Education - Master’s degree (M.A.) in Counseling Psychology, Social Work, Clinical Psychology, Mental Health Counseling or related clinical area; five or more years of related experience . Demonstrated high degree of sensitivity, understanding, ability, knowledge, and experience working with students from diverse ethnic, cultural, and socioeconomic backgrounds. Experience - Previous experience working with college students and an awareness of developmental perspective is preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including experience and ability to give group presentations. Demonstrated excellence in organizational skill set, including attention to detail and thorough record-keeping ability. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting lightweight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average-weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Licenses/Certifications Must currently possess full licensure or be on track to obtain full licensure for practice in the State of Michigan. Preference will be given to candidates with current licensure. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Mon to Fri, 8:30 AM to 5:00 PM"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001215382506": {
      "title": "Data and Reporting Specialist",
      "description": "Data and Reporting Specialist. Position Classification FT Staff Position Summary The Data/Reporting Specialist assists the Advancement Systems Manager in maintaining data integrity for a large alumni/donor database, supporting fundraising and alumni engagement efforts. Key duties include providing accurate data and reports, designing user-specific reports, training staff on the Raiser's Edge system, offering technical support, creating documentation, and managing various reports such as month-end, year-end, and quarterly updates. The role involves data entry, processing deposits, overseeing student workers, and supporting system functions like the NXT portal. The specialist also develops queries and reports, improves documentation, and ensures data accuracy and confidentiality. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Develop reports, queries 10% Month-End Reporting 7% Fupload to Banner 5% Create documentation 3% VSE Yearly Report 5% US New Yearly Report 5% NCOA Quarterly Updates 5% Deceased Finder 5% Deposit Processing 3% Year-end accrual reporting 5% Direct mail data request 15% Assist with in NXT Portal 7% Oversee 1-2 student workers 10% Provide backup support for Advancement Systems Manager 5% Training new & existing staff to ensure correct procedures are followed 5% Provide technical support to University Advancement staff, addressing system-related inquiries and issues 5% Minimum Qualifications Education – A college degree or four to eight years of work experience in a related field. Employment – Four to eight years of work experience in a related field. (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Preferred Qualifications Proficient in Raiser's Edge/NXT Database or other development database experience (3-5 Years of experience). Experience with data processing in a non-profit/high education setting. Experience maintaining CRM data, creating reports, and analyzing data. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills. Proficiency in Excel, working knowledge of Microsoft Word and Outlook required Data Entry Polite customer service skills Good Communication (oral/written), and organizational skills Ability to work in a diverse setting (including University community/donors) Ability to work under deadline pressure with attention to detail and accuracy Ability to multi-task and meet deadlines Ability to dynamically adjust the data output to meet customer requirements. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Mon to Fri, 8:30 AM to 5:00 PM Additional Information Willing and able to learn the job and environment. Maintain Confidentiality. Work effectively and cooperatively as a team member within Department and with all departments. Attend meetings. Observe dress and conduct codes. Meet attendance standards as established and provide proper notice of absence. Perform other duties as assigned by supervisor. Follow proper etiquette and guidelines when responding to emails."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001214390006": {
      "title": "Academic and Clinical Faculty Optometry",
      "description": "Academic and Clinical Faculty Optometry. Position Classification FT Optometry Faculty Position Summary The University of Detroit Mercy School of Optometry invites applications for full-time faculty positions. We welcome a diverse group of applicants with interests in primary care, ocular disease, low vision, contact lenses, vision science, or other specialties who are passionate about teaching and mentoring future optometrists in a collaborative, student-centered, and community-focused environment. Candidates may contribute to clinical instruction, didactic teaching, research, or a combination of these areas, depending on experience and professional interests. Faculty rank will be determined commensurate with qualifications and experience. Early career optometrists will find robust faculty mentorship, onboarding support, and professional development opportunities designed to foster long-term success in academic optometry. The program is located in Novi, Michigan, a vibrant and welcoming suburban community in Metro Detroit. Novi offers excellent schools, diverse dining, abundant recreation, and affordable living relative to many major metropolitan areas. Its proximity to Detroit provides convenient access to world-class cultural institutions, professional sports, and a thriving healthcare and research ecosystem. Novi is consistently ranked among the top places to live in the United States. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Shape the next generation of optometrists through engaging, high-impact teaching and mentorship across didactic, laboratory, and clinical education settings, aligned with program needs and expertise. Participate in the delivery, coordination, and continuous improvement of courses, including development of syllabi, learning objectives, instructional materials, and assessments. Provide timely, constructive, and appropriate feedback to students to support academic and professional development. Participate in the clinical training and supervision of student interns, fostering clinical competence and professionalism. Engage in scholarly activity appropriate to assigned faculty rank and career goals, which may include educational scholarship, clinical research, or professional dissemination. Maintain active participation in local, state, and national optometric organizations, contributing to the profession and staying current with evolving standards of care. Actively participate in program, school, and university committees in support of the mission and goals of the School of Optometry. Foster supportive, professional, and collaborative relationships with faculty, staff, students, and clinical partners. Adopt and advance the mission and goals of the School of Optometry and the University. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the continued growth and success of the School of Optometry. Minimum Qualifications Education – A Doctor of Optometry degree from an ACOE accredited institution. Experience – Completion of an ACOE accredited residency or 3 years of clinical experience. Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching and/or research experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Attention to detail and the ability to work with a team in a fast-paced environment Exceptional organizational skills and an ability to meet deadlines in an efficient manner Computer proficiency, specifically with MS Office and aptitude to learn new computer applications Excellent verbal and written communication skills Excellent interpersonal skills Ability to use independent judgment and maintain confidentiality Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Licenses/Certifications Licensed and in good standing or eligible for optometry licensure in the state of Michigan. Salary/Pay Information Starting annual salary of $120,000, with higher compensation commensurate with experience. Anticipated Schedule The position is available immediately, with a start date as soon as possible or as mutually agreed upon. Faculty assignments determined by program needs, faculty experience, and professional interests"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001213771606": {
      "title": "Director of Law Student Wellbeing",
      "description": "Director of Law Student Wellbeing. Position Classification FT Admin Position Summary Consistent with Detroit Mercy Law’s commitment to educating the complete lawyer through the Jesuit and Mercy traditions of service, justice, compassion, and care for the whole person, the Director of Law Student Wellbeing leads the law school’s holistic approach to supporting student flourishing, spiritually, emotionally, intellectually, and professionally. Serving 650+ residential and online JD students, the Director provides clinical mental health support, partners in integrating wellbeing throughout the curriculum, advances a compassionate and inclusive school culture, supports faculty and staff as educators and mentors, and engages in scholarship that strengthens the field of wellbeing in legal education. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Direct Student Support & Clinical Consultation. Provide clinical therapeutic mental health consults, short-term counseling, crisis intervention, and triage for both residential and online JD students. Maintain high ethical standard clinical records and ensure appropriate confidentiality and compliance. Collaborate with university clinicians, disability services, community mental health providers, and student affairs team to support care continuity. Provide targeted well being programming during peak stress periods such as 1L transition, exams, and bar preparation. Organizational Culture & Community Wellbeing. Lead schoolwide initiatives that promote an inclusive culture of wellness. Use data informed strategies to identify systemic stressors and implement improvements that support a professional learning community. Partner with DEIB leadership to ensure equitable access to wellbeing resources and responsive support for historically marginalized student populations. Provide training on trauma-informed teaching, supporting distressed students, and cultivating professional identity in ways consistent with Jesuit & Mercy values. Curricular Integration of Wellness Principles. Partner with faculty integrating wellbeing, resilience, professional identity formation, and trauma-informed practice into courses, clinics, externships, and orientation. Develop workshops and modules that help students understand the relationship between mental health, ethics, professionalism, and effective lawyering. Serve as a consultant to faculty in designing teaching practices that support equitable and healthy learning environments consistent with Jesuit pedagogy. Scholarship, Assessment & Professional Leadership. Engage in scholarship related to law student well being, mental health, identity formation, ethics, or legal education practices. Represent Detroit Mercy Law at conferences, associations, and professional communities focused on wellness and legal education. Assess wellbeing initiatives and prepare reports for accreditation, strategic planning, and leadership review. Stay informed about emerging trends in professional school mental health, student development, and regulatory standards. JOB REQUIREMENTS SECTION Minimum Qualifications Education – A college degree and a professional certificate or graduate degree; or 10 or more years of work experience in a related field. Employment - Two years to five years (Equivalent combination of Education and employment). Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree (M.A.) in Counseling Psychology, Clinical Psychology, Counseling, Social Work, or related clinical area; five or more years of related experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Flexible in meeting the needs of a graduate proffesional students in terms of availability, schedule modifications, modality of therapeutic intervention, and referrals on an ongoing basis. Demonstrated ability to navigate complex issues involving mental health triage and response within the context of a higher education environment. Previous experience working with college or professional students and an awareness of developmental perspective is preferred. Willingness to engage and interact in a dynamic and inclusive educational environment with a social justice and equity-minded approach. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Licenses/Certifications Must currently possess full licensure Licensed Professional Counselor (LPC) Licensed Psychologist (LP) Licensed Master Social Worker - Clinical (LMSW) Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Monday to Friday 8.30 AM to 5.00 PM. Additional Information This is a full-time position with all job responsibilities occurring at the School of Law. This position includes routine collaboration with the Student Health & Wellness Center at the University of Detroit Mercy on university-wide initiatives and case-by-case consultations, as needed."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001216649706": {
      "title": "Public Safety Officer",
      "description": "Public Safety Officer. Position Classification FT Staff (MAP) Essential Duties and Responsibilities Patrols campus, providing security to all individuals on university property; checks and maintains security to all buildings and grounds. Provides security services (unlocking cars, starting stalled vehicles, emergency weather notification, unlocking/locking doors to buildings, etc.) Monitors facilities and reports any problems to Physical Plant for repair. Investigates university criminal or traffic complaints/concerns. Deals with parking concerns and enforcement. Assumes specified responsibilities in the Director's absence. Attends training sessions or meetings required by the Director. Monitors students working security during assigned shift. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Education - A high school diploma or GED Employment - Five to seven years of experience in a related field. (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Preferred Qualifications Courtesy, tact, and diplomacy are essential elements of the job. Work involves extensive personal contact with others inside and/or outside the university for the purpose of giving or obtaining information, building relationships, or soliciting cooperation. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities A professional, patient demeanor that promotes a positive impression with co-workers and the University Community. Must have strong organizational and administrative skills, a good work ethic, and a positive attitude for interacting with other people. Strong communication skills, verbal and written. Computer proficiency in MS Word/Excel/Access is required with a strong computer aptitude for learning various computer applications; Must be adaptable with the ability to accept and support change, highly skilled at multitasking and detail-oriented, able to effectively work independently or in a team environment, and able to work well under pressure. Demonstrate a professional demeanor and a clean well-groomed appearance that creates a positive impression with customers and coworkers. Must be dependable, reliable, and confident working in a professional environment. 5 Years experience in Law Enforcement at State, Federal, or Military service with discipline in Law Enforcement Excellent Organizational Skills, Excellent Presentation Skills, Exercise Independent Judgement, Self-Motivated, Strong Interpersonal Communication, Demonstrate ability to resolve conflict providing an acceptable resolution, Effective time management skills. Ability to digest policy & procedural information and effectively communicate them to employees. Physical Requirements Lifting, carrying, pushing and/or dragging objects weighing up to 200 lbs. (200+ in some situations), 10 feet or less; running, jumping and climbing various inclines, elevated surfaces, terrains, and/or obstacles; subject to toxic chemicals, fumes, and/or odors; exposed to infectious diseases. Work Environment Regular exposure to unfavorable conditions such as weather conditions, or confined, noisy, or dirty locations. Licenses/Certifications MCOLES certification/Certifiable or 5 years of experience in Law Enforcement at State, Federal, Military Service, or college or university public safety department, Police Department, or Campus Security Department. A valid driver’s license with a good driving record. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule TBD Note - The posting is currently available for a MAP team members."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001217426306": {
      "title": "Clinic Receptionist",
      "description": "Clinic Receptionist. Position Classification FT Staff Non-Union Position Summary The clinic receptionist will assist with the day-to-day needs of the University of Detroit Mercy Eye Institute’s clinical functioning. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Performs all duties of a Clinic receptionist including, but not limited to, answering telephones, patient check-in, patient check-out, collecting patient demographic and insurance information, insurance verification, payment collection, posting charges/payments to EMR, daily deposit balancing, and preparing daily bank deposits. Participates in clinical Risk Management, Quality Assurance, Compliance, and Patient Safety/Infection Control Programs. Patient appointment management which includes scheduling, confirmation of appointments, triaging incoming calls, and management of missed appointments. Assists interns and faculty with insurance and payment related questions. Assists interns and faculty with billing, coding, and posting charges to EHR. Ensures the front desk and waiting room area are clean and presentable. Communicates effectively with patients, solving concerns politely, promptly and effectively. Communicates effectively and professionally with all faculty, students, and staff members. Assists with all aspects of clinic functions including optical and technician duties when needed. Other duties as assigned or as needs arise relating to the effective implementation of the clinical program. Minimum Qualifications Education – A High School Diploma or GED. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule TBD"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001217391906": {
      "title": "Appointment or Receptionist Manager",
      "description": "Appointment or Receptionist Manager. Position Classification FT Administrator Position Summary Supervise Graduate Clinic Coordinators (Periodontics, Oral Surgery, AEGD), ADP Coordinator, Pediatric Coordinator, Telecommunications, and Reception. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Supervising the Telecommunications Monitor patient calls to assure patients are greeted in a friendly and professional manner. Monitor patient calls to confirm patients are receiving accurate information. Assure appointments are scheduled correctly with the provider and clinic. Assure staff is correcting patient information based on reports (patient unsubscribed and blank or incorrect number) provided by Easy Market. Ensure staff is following script when scheduling screening appointments. Assure staff is following protocol for pre-registration and the patient information is accurate. Supervising the Reception Assure patients and visitors are greeted in a friendly and professional manner. Assure patients of record are encouraged to use the kiosk for check-in. Assure patients are receiving accurate information. Assure staff is following protocol for new patients’ appointments. Supervising Staff Ensure staff is following the Dental Center attendance policy. Ensure there is adequate coverage for daily operations in the coordinator clinics, telecommunications, and reception areas. Hire, train, discipline and dismiss staff as necessary. Review and approve time cards. Supervising Coordinators Assure patients and visitors are greeted in a friendly and professional manner. Assure patients appointments are scheduled accurately. Assure patients calls are returned in a timely manner. Assure patients are signing treatment plans before treatment and receiving accurate information related to their planned treatment. Administrative Responsibilities Assist with schedules (Graduate Clinics, Emergency, and Screening). Medical consults for clinics (Graduate and Undergraduate Clinics). Assist with the financial staff when needed. Minimum Qualifications Education : A high school diploma or GED (*recently updated). Employment: Five years to seven years (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Thorough knowledge of dental procedures Organizational skills Previous supervisory experience Strong communication skills Strong problem-solving skills Ability to motivate and build a quality team Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Mon to Fri, 8:30 AM to 5:00 PM"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001211629806": {
      "title": "Associate Head Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Associate Head Athletic Trainer. Position Classification FT Administrator Position Summary Assist in the administration of the Athletic Department's Sports Medicine Department that adheres to all University, Conference, and NCAA rules and regulations while providing a safe and accepting environment for coaches, staff, and student-athletes to grow and develop academically, athletically and encourages personal responsibility, sportsmanship, and service to others. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Treats injuries and recommends medical attention for athletes injured in sporting events. Provides injury preventative education to athletes and coaches and also provides rehabilitation of injuries through nutrition counseling and/or physical activities. Prepares necessary paperwork related to injury reports, insurance reports, training manuals, and budget needs. Organizes student-athlete physicals prior to sport participation and maintains student-athlete medical files. Perform other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Education – A college degree or four to eight years of work experience in a related field. Employment – Six months to two years of work experience in an administrative role. (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Well-polished communication and interpersonal skills Excellent leadership and motivational skills Willing and able to drive 15-passenger vans Physical Requirements Job requires repetitive lifting of light weight objects with frequent bending and stooping, or repetitively lift average weight objects where frequent bending or stooping alternates with lighter activities. Occasionally lifts heavy objects (over 50 pounds). Work Environment Occasional exposure to objectionable conditions or variations such as those found in variable weather conditions or light industrial settings. Willing and able to travel extensively. Licenses/Certifications Valid Driver's License; BOC Certified Athletic Trainer; State of Michigan Athletic Training License; American Red Cross First Aid Certification Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Monday – Friday, 8:30 AM to 5:30 PM willing and able to work evenings and weekends. Additional Information Willing and able to travel extensively; willing and able to work evenings and weekends."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001211355106": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant. Position Classification FT-Staff UDMPSSA (Grade 9 Position) Position Summary This job’s focus is to provide administrative support to the Department of Biology in the College of Engineering, Science, and the Ford Life Sciences Building. The department serves approximately 700 major students, 18 full-time faculty, a Laboratory Manager, and 2 Instructor/Adjunct employees. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provides confidential administrative support to faculty and staff regarding degree-granting programs. Collects and prepares information for use in discussions and meetings. Resolves problems that have an impact on the overall efficiency and running of the Life Sciences Building and the course offerings of the Biology department. For example: facilities and IT ticket submissions, class cancellations, faculty announcement. Screens incoming mail, publications, and other correspondence for faculty and staff in the department. Prepares or assists in the collection of information and data for departmental reports, dean requested data. Assists with Graduation and Honor convocation preparation. Assists in program planning, development, and execution of departmental and college activities/ events. Prepares, writes, and disseminates a monthly departmental newsletter to communication departmental activities to faculty and staff within the department/college. Assists in entering departmental courses for upcoming semester into Coursedog. Maintains daily appointment calendar for the Departmental Chair and Assistant Chair; communicates information regarding cancellations or changes. Coordinates meetings and makes appointments when necessary. Performs other duties as needed or assigned. Minimum Qualifications Education – A high school diploma or GED Employment – Six months to two years of work experience (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Physical Requirements The job may require lifting light-weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions, such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information UDMPSSA Grade 9 Position $22.6284 per hour. Anticipated Schedule 8:30 AM to 5:00 PM Note - This position is currently available for UDMPSSA union members."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001212546306": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant Online JD and Academic Success",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant Online JD and Academic Success. Position Classification FT Staff Non-union Position Summary The Administrative Assistant supports the Online JD and Academic Success. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Online JD Administrative Support: Provide administrative support to faculty, deans, and directors in the Online JD Program. Support faculty and adjunct faculty with course management, including providing basic technological assistance when needed Prepare class rosters, course materials, and other correspondence Serve as an exam monitor during the exam period. Provide front desk coverage in the Student Service Center as needed Support Online JD admissions team Academic Success Administrative Support: Support Associate Dean of Student Learning and Assessment, Assistant Dean and Director of Bar Exam Strategies in the in-person and online JD programs. Other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Education – A two-year college degree or completion of a specialized course of study at a business or trade school. Employment - Six months to two years (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Excellent customer service skills Intermediate knowledge of Microsoft Office Close attention to detail Ability to multitask Ability to maintain confidentiality Effective problem-solving skills Ability to prioritize and consistently meet deadlines Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience. Anticipated Schedule Monday to Friday 8.30 AM to 5.00 PM."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001212571306": {
      "title": "Career Services Director Online JD",
      "description": "Career Services Director Online JD. Position Classification FT Admin Position Summary Direct career services and outreach to support student and graduate employment outcomes for the online JD program and accomplish career-related organizational goals, including supporting strategic employer outreach for the career services office. Create and implement strategic plans, track and report results, ensure compliance with ABA and NALP standards. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Services & Outreach for Online JD students Direct services and outreach to support online students and graduates with securing legal experience. Create career-related educational resources, conduct career-related programming, facilitate networking, provide individualized counseling, assist with preparing resumes and other application materials, conduct mock interviews. Develop and maintain relationships with students, graduates, and employers, identify their needs, and assist them in achieving their objectives. Generate student and graduate employment opportunities through employer research and outreach. Facilitate Early Legal Experience for Online JD students Conduct 1:1 career-planning meetings with first-year online students. Support online students with securing legal experience during law school. Partner with externship program. Track and report outcomes. Graduate Employment Outcomes for Online JD students Direct services and outreach to support online graduate employment in bar passage required and JD advantage positions. Track and report at-graduation and 10 months post-graduation employment outcomes. Ensure graduate employment data is accurately collected and reported in compliance with ABA and NALP requirements. Other Duties Collaborate within CSO and across law school departments. Maintain knowledge of legal industry/market, career and professionalism trends, and best practices. Complete strategic employer research and outreach projects. Support colleagues as needed. Other duties as assigned. JOB REQUIREMENTS SECTION Minimum Qualifications Education – A doctorate degree JD Employment – Two year to five year (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Preferred Qualifications High attention to detail required. Superior communication skills required. Grammar and organizational skills required. Must possess a professional appearance. Must possess a service attitude. Must possess the ability to multi-task in a distracting environment and meet deadlines. Must be self-motivated and innovative. Must possess strong problem-solving skills and the ability to quickly learn new skills, including technological skills. Ability to maintain strict confidentiality required. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Technology skills required. Proficiency with Office products, including, but not limited to, Word, PowerPoint, Outlook, and Excel. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Monday to Friday 8.30 AM to 5.00 PM"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001211190906": {
      "title": "Clinical Coordinator Physician Assistant Program",
      "description": "Clinical Coordinator Physician Assistant Program. Position Classification FT Administrator Position Summary The key responsibility of this position is the planning, preparation, and successful process of clinical rotations for Physician Assistant students. This position consults, collaborates and plans activities with the PA Director of Clinical Education (DCE), PA Program Director, PA faculty, College of Health Professions’ Clinical Education and Compliance Officer, and external clinical partners. This position communicates effectively with students and responds to their needs and concerns. This position works with all other key stakeholders including affiliated hospitals, medical practices, preceptors, and partners to coordinate compliance paperwork for specific clinical placement requirements and to ensure preceptor vetting and communication. This position requires a flexible schedule to assure the needs of the program are met. Occasional evening and weekend hours may be expected. Essential Duties and Responsibilities 1) Clinical Administration Collaborates with the PA DCE, PA Program Director, PA Faculty, and clinical coordinators to obtain specific student clinical requirements, then uses the information to accurately coordinate plans, and manage assigned tasks for clinical placements for students required to meet graduation criteria Forecasts clinical placement requirements based on student enrollment data and coordinate with directors the scheduling of the clinical placements well in advance Communicates with clinical sites to obtain and manage the required documents and assures they are all current and acquired as needed Responds to requests from the PA DCE, PA Program Director, Faculty, Compliance Officer, and clinical coordinators to change or modify placements. Engages actively with clinical coordinators to establish and maintain successful relationships, including site visits as required. Develops and implements innovative approaches to improve methods of clinical placement and obtaining compliance documents. Assist with onboarding and training of students to the clinical database systems. Responsible for the coordination of the PA students’ ‘end of rotation days’ clinical activities and assist as required. Collaborate with the program faculty to assure a smooth interface between the clinical and didactic phases of the program 2) Database Management Schedule student clinical placements in the database platforms & spreadsheets. Routinely maintains updates of clinical sites and preceptors. Executes rotation requests into ACEMAPP database when necessary. Maintains and oversees applicable preceptors payments on an ongoing basis. Train and become a source expert on platforms related to the program and clinical year. 3) Administrative Attend all team meetings and other meetings as required including the annual faculty retreat. Provides meeting minutes with clinical year team meetings. Collaborate with the clinical coordinators from affiliated hospitals and clinical sites to assure effective communication. Identifies all preceptor payments and monitors payment activities to assure timely stipends are processed (or continued medical education credits) as applicable. Assists the PA DCE, program director, and clinical faculty in updating handbooks, documents, etc. as assigned Coordinate obtaining electronic and/or handwritten evaluations and documents as assigned and processes all information related to clinical rotations in the database platforms as required. Collaboratively create and maintain a preceptor recognition process. 4) Other duties as assigned by the Dean, the Associate dean of the school of Health and Rehabilitation Sciences, and the PA Program Director. Clinical Coordination • Collaborates with appropriate faculty clinical coordinators to obtain specific student clinical requirements, then uses the information to accurately plan, develop and manage multiple clinical placements per student • Forecasts clinical placement requirements based on student enrollment data • Negotiates clinical site placements • Responds to requests from faculty clinical coordinators to change placements • Develops and implements innovative approaches to improve methods to clinical placement • Assist with onboarding students to the clinical database system (Typhon) Database Management • Schedule student clinical placements in the database (Typhon) • Maintain and routinely update database of clinical sites and preceptors (Typhon) • Enter rotation requests into the ACEMAPP database when necessary • Maintains and updates preceptor database Administrative • Attend all PA clinical year team meetings • Submit invoices for preceptor payments • Assist faculty clinical coordinators in updating handbooks, documents, etc. • Coordinate electronic evaluations • Organize preceptor recognition • Other duties as assigned JOB REQUIREMENTS SECTION Minimum Qualifications A. Bachelor’s degree or higher required B. Minimum of two years of experience in healthcare management and or administrative roles C. Highly organized with the ability to work under short deadlines E. Skilled in multitasking and managing multiple, competing, and changing priorities F. Proficient in word processing, spreadsheet creation, and related software applications G. Demonstrates initiative and a proactive approach to supporting student and program needs H. Willingness to maintain a flexible schedule to meet program needs Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree. Experience within a higher education institution. Prior Clinical Education experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to maintain professional relationships with clinical partners Possesses professional communications skills, both written and verbal Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously and manage time to meet established deadlines Ability to make decisions within the university’s policies and procedures Self-motivated and willing to take on new projects Able to work independently and collaboratively Excellent attention to detail Database management experience required Experience using a database such as Typhon, Exxat, Complio, and ACEMAPP ideal, but not required Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light-weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Licenses/Certifications A valid driver’s license is required. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Monday – Friday 8:30 am – 5:00 pm"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001209935506": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Annual Giving",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Annual Giving. Position Classification FT Administrator Position Summary The University of Detroit Mercy seeks an enthusiastic and dedicated Assistant Director of Annual Giving to join our Advancement team. This position plays a crucial role in fostering a culture of philanthropy within the university community by managing student philanthropy initiatives, including the senior class gift campaign, young alumni engagement, parent giving, employee giving, the matching gift program, and reunion giving. The Assistant Director will work collaboratively with various stakeholders to achieve annual fundraising goals, enhance donor engagement, and promote a lifelong commitment to the university. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Student Philanthropy: Lead and manage the senior class gift campaign, working closely with graduating students to encourage participation and instill a tradition of giving. Develop and implement programs to educate and engage students in philanthropy, fostering a spirit of generosity and involvement from the freshman year through graduation. Coordinate events and activities that promote student giving and recognize student donors. Young Alumni Engagement: Develop and implement strategies to engage young alumni (graduates from the last decade) in the university’s annual giving programs. Create and manage events, communications, and campaigns specifically targeted at young alumni to foster continued connection and support. Work with young alumni volunteers and advisory groups to increase participation and cultivate future leadership donors. Parent Giving: Design and execute strategies to engage parents in the university's philanthropic efforts, encouraging their support for various university initiatives. Collaborate with the Parents Council and other parent volunteer groups to strengthen relationships and increase parent participation in giving. Employee Giving: Oversee the university's employee giving program, encouraging faculty and staff to support the institution through charitable contributions. Develop and implement initiatives to increase employee participation and recognize employee donors. Matching Gift Program: Manage the matching gift program, working with donors and their employers to maximize the impact of their contributions. Promote the matching gift program to alumni, parents, employees, and friends of the university to increase awareness and participation. Reunion Giving: Coordinate reunion giving programs, working with alumni celebrating milestone reunions to encourage special gifts in honor of their class. Develop and implement strategies to engage reunion classes, including personalized outreach, events, and recognition opportunities. Collaborate with the Alumni Relations team to integrate reunion activities with fundraising efforts, maximizing participation and support. General Responsibilities: Assist in the development and execution of annual giving campaigns, including direct mail, email, social media, and other communication channels. Work with the Director of Annual Giving to identify and cultivate prospective donors, leveraging data and analytics to inform strategies. Collaborate with colleagues in the Advancement team and other university departments to support comprehensive fundraising initiatives. Maintain accurate records of donor interactions and contributions in the university's CRM, Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT and RE7, system. Prepare reports and analyses to evaluate the effectiveness of annual giving programs and make recommendations for improvement. Represent the university at events and activities, both on and off-campus, to promote the university's mission and fundraising goals. JOB REQUIREMENTS SECTION Minimum Qualifications Education – A college degree. Employment – Six months to two years of work experience. (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong Interpersonal Skills: Empathy and Active Listening: Ability to understand and relate to the unique needs and experiences of students and young alumni. Relationship Building: Skilled in building and maintaining relationships, which is essential for fostering long-term engagement and support. Communication Skills: Effective Communication: Proficient in both written and verbal communication, able to articulate the institution’s mission, values, and needs clearly. Social Media Savvy: Knowledgeable about various social media platforms and how to use them effectively to engage with a younger audience. Engagement and Outreach: Event Planning: Experience in organizing events that appeal to students and young alumni. Creative Engagement Strategies: Ability to develop innovative approaches to engage employees, parents, young alumni and current students in meaningful ways. Understanding of Higher Education Landscape: Knowledge of Institutional Priorities: Awareness of the institution’s strategic goals and how employee, parent, student and alumni engagement fit into these objectives. Familiarity with Student Experience: Insight into the current student experience and challenges, allowing for relevant and impactful programming and communication. Fundraising Skills: Annual Giving Programs: Understanding of annual giving and how to inspire giving among employees, parents, students and recent graduates. Cultivation and Stewardship: Skills in cultivating new donors and stewarding existing ones, particularly among the young alumni demographic. Analytical and Data-Driven: Data Analysis: Ability to use data to track engagement metrics, identify trends, and measure the success of outreach efforts. CRM, Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT and RE7, Proficiency: Proficiency with customer relationship management (Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT and RE7) systems to manage interactions and engagement history. Team Collaboration: Collaboration: Ability to work effectively with various departments, including alumni relations and academic units, to coordinate efforts. Leadership and Initiative: Demonstrates leadership and takes initiative in developing new programs and strategies for engagement. Adaptability and Problem-Solving: Flexibility: Capable of adapting to changing circumstances and needs, whether it’s adjusting engagement strategies or addressing unforeseen challenges. Problem-Solving: Proactive in identifying issues and developing solutions to improve employee, parent, student and young alumni experiences. Passion for Education and Student Success: Commitment to Education: Deep passion for higher education and a commitment to supporting student success and lifelong learning. Advocacy for Students and Alumni: Acts as an advocate for students and alumni, understanding their needs and working to address them through institutional resources and support. Cultural Competence: Diversity and Inclusion: Understanding and appreciation of diverse backgrounds and perspectives, ensuring that engagement efforts are inclusive and equitable. Global Perspective: Awareness of global trends and the ability to engage international students and alumni effectively. Physical Requirements The job may require lifting light-weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions, such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information $50,000-$55,000 Annually Anticipated Schedule 8 AM to 5 PM"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001209926906": {
      "title": "DCDC Designer",
      "description": "DCDC Designer. Position Classification FT Administrator Position Summary The Designer will be an integral part of the DCDC team and will be responsible for the day-to-day development of project documents and deliverables. Essential Duties and Responsibilities General office administration Work on community-engaged design projects, including design development, graphic representation, community engagement and production of draft and final deliverables. Manage select assigned projects after 9 to 12 months and with support from senior DCDC staff. JOB REQUIREMENTS SECTION Minimum Qualifications Education – A college degree or four to eight years of work experience in a related field. Employment – None Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Must be familiar with Adobe Suite, Rhino, Excel, Microsoft Teams, and Revit, and/or AutoCAD Ability to collaborate with internal project teams Ability to collaborate with the community Highly organized and self-directed Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Occasional exposure to objectionable conditions or variations such as those found in variable weather conditions or light industrial settings. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Monday to Friday 8.00 AM to 5.00 PM Documents Required Please upload a copy of your portfolio for application consideration."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001209923906": {
      "title": "Senior Designer Project Director",
      "description": "Senior Designer Project Director. Position Classification FT Administrator Position Summary A Senior Designer & Project Director is responsible for directing select projects and initiatives and the day-to-day management and development of those projects and initiatives. The scope of the position includes: implement the mission, vision, goals, and values of the Design Center through project and special initiative direction, management, development and coordination of the community engaged design process, design development and coordination at all phases of a project and initiative, contributing to DCDC business and fund development by identifying and securing new projects and grants, and overseeing other staff assigned to projects and initiatives for which the Project Director is responsible. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Office administration Directing and managing projects, overseeing production and reviewing all project materials and deliverables, developing project materials and final deliverables Managing and overseeing junior staff and students assigned to the Project Director's projects Mentoring junior staff and students assigned to the Project Director's projects Business and Fund Development - identifying and securing new project contracts and grants, writing project and grant proposals JOB REQUIREMENTS SECTION Minimum Qualifications Education – A college degree or four to eight years of work experience in a related field. Employment – Seven years to ten years. (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Preferred Qualifications Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Architectural design Ability to work collaboratively with organizations, community groups and individuals across Detroit’s neighborhoods Strong project management skills Strong ability to manage junior staff assigned to projects Business and fund development experience Must be familiar with Adobe Suite, Rhino, Excel, Microsoft Teams, and Revit and/or AutoCAD. Physical Requirements The job may require lifting light-weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Occasional exposure to objectionable conditions or variations such as those found in variable weather conditions or light industrial settings. Licenses/Certifications Architecture license a plus Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Monday – Friday, 8:30 a.m. – 5:00 p.m. Document Required Please upload a copy of your portfolio for application consideration."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001210024406": {
      "title": "Director of Development Law",
      "description": "Director of Development Law. Position Classification FT Administrator Position Summary The Director of Development for the School of Law (SOL) is responsible for planning and managing the overall major gift work for the SOL. They will work through University Advancement (UA) and in conjunction with the Dean to advance the priorities of the academic unit as well as the University. The Director of Development, SOL will be responsible for developing and implementing an overall major gift program that will support the specific academic area initiatives and the University of Detroit Mercy’s overall development efforts. Focusing on major gift commitments, the DOD identifies, qualifies, cultivates and solicits prospects, and stewards donors, according to the performance expectations established in UA. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Identification of donor prospects. Contact with donors and donor prospects for qualification, cultivation, solicitation and stewardship. Actively work all four stages of their assigned portfolio of prospects. Contact preparation and follow-up, contact reports, proposal development. Detailing of monthly and annual metrics for performance centered around in-person meetings, quality outreach, and annual fundraising goals. Meetings with Dean, faculty, staff and UA supervisor and UA team. Other duties that support major gift development. Requirements Minimum Qualifications Education – A college degree or four to eight years of work experience in a related field. Employment – Five years to seven years (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Preferred Qualifications Employee will have sound knowledge of laws, best practices and philosophy of charitable giving. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The employee will have the knowledge and skills to successfully manage a portfolio of major gift prospects and donors for the University’s fundraising initiatives. Knowledge and skills include the ability to identify, qualify and cultivate donor prospects; to develop timely and effective solicitation strategies; to conduct personal solicitations; and to effectively steward donors in a way that will lead to their next gift. Employee will have the knowledge and skills to develop fundraising goals and detailed prospect strategy plans with priorities, action steps, timelines and expected outcomes; to maintain complete contact reports and appropriate Raiser’s Edge records; and to advise on the development of fundraising marketing materials. Employee will have the ability to work with the Dean and appropriate faculty and staff to develop and maintain a comprehensive approach to external relations, and to fulfill the major gift portion of that plan, which will include, but not be limited to, assisting the Dean with local, regional, and national strategies to increase both the amount of monies raised and the number of donors giving to the school. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Monday – Friday, 8:30 am -5:00 pm Additional Information Employee must possess a commitment to support and articulate the University’s Catholic, Jesuit and Mercy mission; have excellent verbal and written communication skills; have appropriate computer skills in support of fundraising; have the interpersonal skills to work effectively with major gift prospects and donors, volunteers and University leaders; and have the ability to contribute to University Advancement as part of the Major Gift Team."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001208331006": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Lecturer. Position Classification FT Faculty UDMPU (9 month) Position Summary The Department of Religious Studies at the University of Detroit Mercy invites applications for a full-time non-tenure-track position at the rank of Lecturer in Health Care Ethics, to begin August 16, 2026. Successful candidates will demonstrate the ability to teach health care ethics from both secular and religious perspectives. Special consideration will be given to candidates who can also teach courses in global health and healing traditions, and other courses in religion and ethics. Candidates shall have Ph.D. or Th.D. in Religious Studies, Theology, or Ethics. Advanced ABDs will be considered. The Lecturer will teach our undergraduate Religious Studies majors and minors, as well as contribute to the university's Core Curriculum in Ethics and Religious Studies. They will teach courses focused on Healthcare Ethics, as well as other courses on topics in their area of specialization. The teaching load is 24 credit hours (8 courses) per academic year. We are especially interested in applicants dedicated to excellence in teaching in a liberal arts setting. Strong candidates will have a record of experience or demonstrated commitment to teaching diverse students. The Department of Religious Studies is deeply committed to the University’s distinctive mission of educational excellence to a diverse student population within a vibrant urban context, a commitment to community engagement, and enhancing diversity, equity, and inclusion in the University community and curriculum. The University’s mission can be found at https://www.udmercy.edu/about/mission-vision/ . Information about the Department of Religious Studies is posted on our website: https://liberalarts.udmercy.edu/academics/rels/index.php . Requirements Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. or Th.D. in Religious Studies, Theology, or Ethics (advance ABDs will be considered). Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience in Health Care Ethics Teaching experience in courses in health care and healing traditions from diverse religious perspectives Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience. Anticipated Schedule TBD Required Application Materials Letter of application stating the applicant’s interest in the position and sharing their experience with and approach to undergraduate teaching. The letter should also reflect on how their teaching, service, and/or community engagement resonates with one or more aspects of Detroit Mercy’s mission and core values . Curriculum vitae. Sample syllabi or detailed course proposals. Teaching statement, including: Pedagogical philosophy. Strategies for working with diverse student populations. DEI (diversity, equity, and inclusion) statement. Official graduate transcripts (or copy of official graduate transcripts). Questions regarding this position or application materials should be directed to Todd Hibbard, Ph.D., chair of the Religious Studies Department: hibbarja@udmercy.edu. Candidates should complete an application and upload materials. Review of applications will begin March 31, 2026, and will continue until an appointment is made."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001208215306": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant IACDE Alum Rel and Comm",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant IACDE Alum Rel and Comm. Position Classification FT Staff Non Union Position Summary Performs professional administrative management and support duties to support the department’s daily operations; assists in program planning and development; interprets, monitors, and analyzes information regarding operating policies and procedures; administers budgets; and coordinates academic and/or staff personnel matters. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Course Planning and Administration: Assist in the implementation and administration of continuing dental education courses. Manage the online course registration and database system, Learning Stream. Maintain all CE course files. Prepare and compile all course materials, including handouts and course evaluations. Run and compile results from course evaluations to be forwarded to course presenters. Facilitate CE courses when required, including setting up audiovisual equipment, monitoring and hosting online courses, monitoring food service, gathering course evaluations, and issuing credit letters. Assist individuals with registrations for courses as needed. Prepare credit letters for all courses. Marketing: Assist in engaging all stakeholders in School of Dentistry news and events through various general web, print-based, and social media outlets. Assist in the preparation and editing of marketing and promotional materials, such as target mailings of course brochures and postcards. Assist in the online promotion of CE courses and alumni events through digital communication and social media. Financial: Settle financial transactions by paying invoices to vendors associated with all CE courses and alumni events. Monitor the budget and prepare purchase orders in Banner associated with all courses and events, and office operations. Prepare and submit check requests and payroll authorizations for all courses, alumni events, and office operations. Maintain a log of checks and purchase orders and verify payments received. Reconcile all credit card transactions with a monthly P-card report. Prepare profit/loss statements for each course and event. General Administration: Enter alumni attendance for events and courses into Raiser’s Edge. Prepare monthly mailings to alumni for milestone birthdays. Monitor and respond to emails sent to the department as needed. Order and maintain all needed office supplies and stationery. Perform other duties as assigned. Requirements Minimum Qualifications Education -A two-year college degree or completion of a specialized course of study at a business or trade school or 18 months to four years of work experience in a related field. Experience – Five years to seven years (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Preferred Qualifications Five to seven years’ experience in office administration. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Computer skills: proficiency with MS Office. Experience producing reports. Excellent written and spoken communication skills. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Monday – Friday, 8:30 a.m. – 5:00 p.m."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001208128706": {
      "title": "Lieutenant",
      "description": "Lieutenant. Position Classification FT Administrator Position Summary To command and direct the entire investigative section and operational section of the Department of Public Safety Department at the University of Detroit Mercy. The training and educating the entire Department of Public Safety and University community through active seminars, and consistent enforcement of all City, State, Federal Laws and University Policy and Procedures. The omission of specific statements of the duties does not exclude them from the classification if work is similar, related, or a logical assignment of position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Ensure that all personnel are properly trained in the performance of their related job, while monitoring and evaluating their performance, and take corrective action as needed. (OIC Department Training Section). Ensure that all shifts and events are appropriately staffed and that all personnel are briefed on situations and conditions, which require their attention. Respond to situations, of a high profile in nature, which necessitates the presence of a Lieutenant for immediate and crucial decisions. Review all reports on a daily basic and ensure that all incidents are investigated and proper reports are generated with the appropriate corrective actions.( OIC of Investigation Section). Monitor crime trends and prepare reports for statistical purposes and to eliminate opportunities or foreseeable risks. Consistent update and review of all departmental policy, procedures and practices to ensure the departmental strives to meet and achieve their goals and objections. Enforce all city, State, and Federal Laws and University Policies and Procedures. Requirements Minimum Qualifications Education – A college degree. Experience – Five years to seven years (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Preferred Qualifications Courtesy, tact, and diplomacy are essential elements of the job. Work involves much personal contact with others inside and/or outside the university for purposes of giving or obtaining information, building relationships, or soliciting cooperation. MCOLES Certified or Certifiable Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities A professional, patient demeanor that promotes a positive impression with co-workers and the University Community. Must have strong organizational and administrative skills, a good work ethic, and a positive attitude for interacting with other people. Strong communication skills, verbal and written. Computer proficiency in MS Word/Excel/Access is required with a strong computer aptitude for learning various computer applications; Must be adaptable with ability to accept and support change, highly skilled at multi-tasking and detailed orientated, able to effectively work independently or in a team environment, and able to work well under pressure. Demonstrate a professional demeanor and a clean well-groomed appearance that creates a positive impression with customers and coworkers. Must be dependable, reliable, and confident working in a professional environment. MCOLES certifiable required. Excellent Organizational Skills, Excellent Presentation Skills, Exercise Independent Judgement, Self-Motivated, Strong Interpersonal Communication Physical Requirements Job requires repetitively lifting average weight objects with repetitive bending and stooping. Frequently lifts heavy objects but alternating with lighter activities. Job may require physical exertion such as long periods of standing. Job may require above-average agility and dexterity. Additional Information Lifting, carrying, pushing and/or dragging objects weighing up to 200 lbs. (200+ in some situations), 10 feet or less; running, jumping and climbing various inclines, elevated surfaces, terrains, and/or obstacles; subject to toxic chemicals, fumes, and/or odors; exposed to infectious diseases. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Varies"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001207864206": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Counseling",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Counseling. Position Summary University of Detroit Mercy Department Counseling program invites applications for a tenure-track position at the assistant or associate professor rank in our nationally-recognized Counseling program to begin August, 2026. The Counseling program offers Master’s programs with specialties in Addiction, Clinical Mental Health, and School Counseling, and a doctoral program to be launched in Fall, 2027. Responsibilities include teaching core courses in the Counseling program, engaging in research and scholarly activities, student advising, curriculum oversight, and providing an array of service activities. Teaching is exclusively and intentionally face-to-face, delivered in our campus-based counseling program in the heart of the city of Detroit. The Counseling program also operates a completely no-cost Counseling Clinic to serve the mental and behavioral health needs of the public while also operating as a teaching Clinic. Typical teaching load includes nine credit hours per semester with a nine-month appointment. Supplemental summer appointments in teaching are also available. Requirements Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Counseling from a CACREP-accredited program within a non-profit, traditional academic institution; Master’s degree in Counseling from a CACREP-accredited program from a non-profit, traditional academic institution; Clinical practice experience; Licensed Professional Counselor/equivalent and/or ability to attain full licensure in Michigan; Potential for or record of successful teaching; Potential for or record of scholarly productivity; Demonstrated commitment to social justice and advocacy. Preferred Qualifications Significant counseling experience excluding practicum and internship; Record of peer-reviewed publication(s) and/or other scholarly publishing; Experience working in an urban environment and/or experience with marginalized individuals. Physical Requirements The job may require lifting lightweight objects (1 to 15 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Work Environment Regular exposure to a standard office and classroom conditions. Salary/Pay Information Rank and salary will be commensurate with experience. The university has excellent benefits including medical and dental insurance, retirement plan with match and tuition benefits for employees and their dependents. Anticipated Schedule Schedule subject to change pending semester workload. Additional Information Consideration of Associate Professor Rank: To be considered for the rank of Associate Professor, applicants must currently hold the rank of Associate Professor . Such applications will be evaluated consistent with department, college, and university criteria for Associate Professor rank that include but are not limited to demonstrated excellence in teaching, a strong record of scholarship, and a record of service at various levels within the University and to the profession. Applications should include : Current CV Names and contact information of 4 references. A letter of interest indicating one’s qualifications for the position. Applications are due June 20, 2026 , and review of applications will begin immediately until the position is filled. Please direct any questions about the position to Dr. Nancy Calleja, Department Chair, at calleyng@udmercy.edu"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001207825906": {
      "title": "Professor of Practice Pediatric Specialty",
      "description": "Professor of Practice Pediatric Specialty. Position Summary The McAuley School of Nursing at the University of Detroit Mercy invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track faculty position with a primary focus on teaching and service. This position supports the School’s mission of educating compassionate, ethical, and clinically competent nurses prepared to serve diverse populations. The successful candidate will contribute to nursing programs through classroom instruction and clinical teaching, and service to the School, University, and profession. The specialty focus for this position is pediatric nursing. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teaching: Provide high-quality instruction and supervision in the classroom and clinical setting. Utilize evidence-based teaching strategies to support student learning and clinical judgment development. Evaluate student performance and provide constructive feedback consistent with course and program outcomes. Participate in curriculum development, implementation, and evaluation. Service: Participate in department, college, and university service activities. Contribute to program accreditation, assessment, and continuous quality improvement efforts. Engage in professional service activities consistent with faculty role expectations. Support student advising, mentoring, and professional development as assigned. Other duties as assigned Requirements Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in nursing from an accredited institution. Current, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license. Clinical expertise in pediatric nursing. Eligibility for RN licensure in the state of Michigan. Prior teaching experience in a nursing program. Preferred Qualifications Familiarity with simulation-based teaching and clinical judgment models Doctoral degree in nursing from an accredited institution. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule TBD"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001207822006": {
      "title": "Professor of Practice",
      "description": "Professor of Practice. Position Summary The McAuley School of Nursing at the University of Detroit Mercy invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track faculty position with a primary focus on teaching and service. This position supports the School’s mission of educating compassionate, ethical, and clinically competent nurses prepared to serve diverse populations. The successful candidate will contribute to both undergraduate and graduate nursing programs through classroom instruction, clinical teaching, and service to the school, university, and profession. The primary clinical focus for this position is medical-surgical nursing. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teaching: Provide high-quality instruction and supervision in the classroom and clinical setting Utilize evidence-based teaching strategies to support student learning and clinical judgment development Evaluate student performance and provide constructive feedback consistent with course and program outcomes. Participate in curriculum development, implementation, and evaluation Service: Participate in department, college, and university service activities- Contribute to program accreditation, assessment, and continuous quality improvement efforts. Engage in professional service activities consistent with faculty role expectations. Support student advising, mentoring, and professional development as assigned. Other duties as assigned Requirements Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in nursing from an accredited institution. Current, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license. Extensive clinical experience in medical-surgical nursing. Eligibility for RN licensure in the state of Michigan – Prior teaching experience in a nursing program. Preferred Qualifications Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) degree or certification. Familiarity with simulation-based teaching and clinical judgement models. Doctoral Degree in Nursing from an accredited institution. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience. Anticipated Schedule TBD"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001207816106": {
      "title": "Professor of Practice MEAGN Program",
      "description": "Professor of Practice MEAGN Program. Position Summary The University of Detroit Mercy, College of Health Professions, McAuley School of Nursing is seeking applicants for the position of Professor of Practice, a full-time non-tenure track position, to support the expansion of our master’s entry advanced generalist nursing (MEAGN) program to West Michigan. The MEAGN program, successfully launched at our Novi campus in 2021, is the first of its kind in Michigan and provides the pathway to nursing for individuals with who hold a baccalaureate degree outside of nursing. The West Michigan campus expects to launch in 2026. The faculty member of the MEAGN program prepares students to provide mission driven, exceptional nursing care and facilitates quality improvement as leaders at the bedside, on the unit, and across the health system. Faculty in the MEAGN Program participate in activities that contribute to both the profession and university mission through teaching, scholarship and service. Key to this role is participation in innovative education strategies in the classroom, skills laboratory, clinical, and simulation center, as part of the MEAGN faculty team. Mentoring students as entry level nurses with an advanced degree is essential for their transition to practice, as well as further education and preparation as advanced nurses. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teaching : Develop content and teach students in didactic, clinical and laboratory courses. Provide students with learning opportunities to develop advanced competencies. Pursue development of teaching strategies that support student achievement of competencies. Clinical coordination to support and develop adjunct faculty while bridging clinical and classroom. Work with the faculty team to develop and participate in innovative teaching strategies, including the Integrated Learning Encounters incorporating simulation. Utilize feedback from course evaluations and key outcome measures such as the NCLEX pass rate to improve student learning. Advising students to enhance and support student success. Includes maintaining records of advising meetings and referrals to appropriate support services. Scholarship: Scholarly work is optional for individuals in the non-tenure Professor of Practice track. Service: Participation in program track, school, college, and/or university shared governance through contributions in committees, taskforces, and other relevant organizations. Participation in student-related organizations and events. Membership and contributions to professional organizations. Mission: Supporting the development of an academically diverse student body. Upholding the mission of the university and McAuley School Nursing through teaching, scholarly and service activities. Other duties as assigned Requirements Minimum Qualifications This individual demonstrates teaching effectiveness in nursing practice. Minimum of Master’s in Nursing and Doctorate is preferred. Licensing/Professional Certifications: Michigan RN license or ability to obtain as well as applicable national nursing certification. Expertise in clinical nursing practice with a minimum or 3 years of clinical practice in a specialty area. Commitment to contribute to clinical learning. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates who have a record of teaching effectiveness in nursing practice. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience. Anticipated Schedule TBD"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001207177306": {
      "title": "Simulation Instructor and Lab Coordinator",
      "description": "Simulation Instructor and Lab Coordinator. Position Summary The University of Detroit Mercy’s Simulation Technology and Research (STAR) Center, located within the College of Health Professions, invites applications for a full-time staff position. This full-time position seeks a highly motivated educator to enhance students’ learning experience through hands-on, simulated activities that promote consistent, positive outcomes. The Simulation Instructor/Lab Coordinator conducts needs assessments, collaborates with faculty to recommend simulation experiences, and designs simulation experiences for students across multidisciplinary programs. This Instructor position is vital to the STAR Center’s mission of improving health and patient safety through simulation-based programs that maximize the abilities of individuals, teams, and systems. The role is ideal for individuals with medical knowledge and a technical interest who are keen to contribute to healthcare education through simulation. The ideal candidate will work with an interprofessional teaching team comprising part-time and full-time faculty and other stakeholders, depending on the level of expertise required to meet the simulation’s learning outcomes. Compensation is based on the role’s level and requirements and is determined by education, experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Instruction & Facilitation Manages and evaluates the facilitation process of simulation experiences on Blackboard and in the STAR Center. Oversees scenario pre-learning, pre-briefing, debriefing, student reflections, and learner evaluation data. Ensures simulation experiences align with didactic course objectives and program outcomes. Provides feedback to learners to promote reflective practice, clinical reasoning, and decision-making skills. Simulation Operations & Equipment Management Collaborates with the simulation technician to develop instructional materials for the setup and use of task trainers, manikins, and other simulation equipment. Maintains awareness of scheduling, availability, and functionality of physical and technical resources for simulation activities. Supports safe and realistic learning environments that align with best practices in healthcare simulation. Curriculum Design & Faculty Collaboration Collaborates with faculty to develop simulation scenarios that promote student learning, critical thinking, and clinical decision-making aligned with course objectives. Uses evidence-based simulation models to design, implement, evaluate, and standardize faculty/staff development programs in simulation-based teaching, debriefing, and assessment. Supports the integration of simulation into the nursing and interprofessional curricula, ensuring alignment with IPEC core competencies and program outcomes. Policy Development & Quality Improvement Assists in the development and revision of policies, procedures, and documentation related to simulation operations, safety, and educational standards. Ensures simulation practices adhere to INACSL Standards of Best Practice: Simulation? and institutional policies. Recommends procedural improvements based on data trends, evaluations, and emerging best practices Program Evaluation, Accreditation & Research Assists the Director of Simulation and IPE with data collection, organization, and reporting required for simulation accreditation (e.g., SSH). Participates in the evaluation and continuous improvement of the simulation program, including scenario effectiveness, learner satisfaction, and institutional alignment. Contributes to research activities, quality improvement projects, and dissemination of simulation outcomes through presentations or scholarly publications. Professional Development & Outreach Maintains current knowledge of best practices, emerging technologies, and standards in simulation-based education. Participates in STAR Center events such as open house, orientation, simulation week, and accepted student day. Leads tours and educational demonstrations for internal and external audiences to promote the STAR Center’s mission and community partnerships. Lab Coordinator Responsibilities Operational Leadership of Nursing Skills Lab Provide day-to-day operational oversight of the nursing skills laboratory. Ensure laboratory readiness, safety, and organization to support student learning. Staff Supervision & Support Hire, orient, and train lab assistants for open labs. Develop lab assistant schedules to meet instructional needs. Inventory & Equipment Management Oversee inventory, ordering, and restocking of supplies and equipment. Sets up and dismantles skills activities, ensuring all equipment, manikins, and supplies are operational and available. Coordinate maintenance and repair of lab equipment and task trainers. Ensure cleanliness and proper storage of lab materials. Monitor budget allocation related to lab supplies. Clinical Absence Oversight Monitor and track clinical absences in accordance with program policy. Communicate with faculty and students regarding absence documentation. Coordinate make-up lab experiences with clinical leadership team. Maintain accurate records for compliance and accreditation Requirements Minimum Qualifications Education – Bachelor of Science in Nursing. Employment – 3 years of experience working in a clinical healthcare role or field. (Equivalent combination of education and employment) Preferred Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing Experience in patient simulation and nursing lab Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Licenses/Certifications Minimum Qualifications: Current State of Michigan Registered Nurse (RN) License American Heart Association Basic Life Support (BLS) Certification Preferred Qualifications: Certified Healthcare Simulation Educator (CHSE) Certification Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Monday to Friday 8.30 AM to 5.00 PM."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001206558006": {
      "title": "Instructor",
      "description": "Instructor. Position Classification FT Faculty UDMPU (9 month) Position Summary The English Department at University of Detroit Mercy seeks applicants for a one-year instructor position with an annual teaching load of eight courses over fall and winter semesters. Teaching assignments are primarily first-year writing (rhetoric and composition) courses with the option of teaching one introductory literature, film, professional writing, or creative writing class per semester. Competitive salary and benefits package. The English department is known for its commitment to excellence in teaching and faculty engagement with undergraduate learners. We welcome nominations of and applications from individuals who would bring additional dimensions to the university’s mission of providing excellent, student-centered education for a diverse student body. Requirements Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree or higher in a related field Demonstrated excellence in teaching in the college setting Knowledge of and commitment to best practices for teaching and mentoring a diverse student body Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in a related field Demonstrated experience helping undergraduate students, including first-generation college students, successfully transition college-level coursework Understanding of and commitment to the university’s mission, including teaching praxis that seeks to integrate students’ intellectual, spiritual, ethical and social development Experience of assessment at the course and/or program level ESL certification and/or significant experience teaching English language learners Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Monday to Friday 8.30 AM to 5.00 PM."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001219145906": {
      "title": "Coordinator Business Ops",
      "description": "Coordinator Business Ops. Position Classification FT Administrator Hourly Essential Duties and Responsibilities Supervise DMPD Interns to ensure the flow of daily routine by updating and implementing policies and procedures; overseeing DMPD Operations departmental budgets; training in the use of the finance side of Banner; monitoring attendance records, personnel files, and key requisitions; and operation of the Front Office daily operations. Supervise DMPD Auxiliary Officer Program by updating and implementing policies and procedures; overseeing DMPD Auxiliary budget; hiring and training; monitoring attendance records and personnel files. Manage DMPD Parking Citation System by maintaining DMPD Parking Enforcement Section to include cross-referencing, verifying, and reconciling Department Citations against departmental tracking detail to find and resolve discrepancies promptly, payment of citation, unpaid citation, Citation Holds Roster, Issuance of student and employee holds and removal. ERP Committee operations coordinator for Chair of ERP or Department Lieutenant. Develop and maintain the Departmental website, to include meeting with DMPD administrators to gather current information; drafting the layout and language for approval; and working in concert with the other DMPD administrator of Jean Clery, Investigation, ERP in creating a current and cohesive website. Provide technical support for various departmental systems to include but not limited to: University Access Control System; serve as contact for the copier and facsimile machines for the area, assisting individuals with problems and contacting the vendor when service or supplies are needed. Perform all other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Education – Some college or with 5 years of experience in an office environment Employment - Six months to two years (Equivalent combination of education and employment). Preferred Qualifications. Excellent Organizational Skills, Excellent Presentation Skills, Exercise Independent Judgement, Self-Motivated, Strong Interpersonal Communication. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities A professional, patient demeanor that promotes a positive impression with co-workers and the University Community. Must have strong organizational and administrative skills, a good work ethic, and a positive attitude for interacting with other people. Strong communication skills, verbal and written. Computer proficiency in MS Word/Excel/Access is required with a strong computer aptitude for learning various computer applications; Banner experience preferred. Must be adaptable with ability to accept and support change, highly skilled at multitasking and detailed orientated, able to effectively work independently or in a team environment, and able to work well under pressure. Demonstrate a professional demeanor and a clean well-groomed appearance that creates a positive impression with customers and coworkers. Must be dependable, reliable, and confident working in a professional environment. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule Mon to Fri, 8:30 AM to 5:00 PM"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001231488306": {
      "title": "Chemistry Lecturer",
      "description": "Chemistry Lecturer. Position Classification FT Faculty UDMPU (9 month). Position Summary The Chemistry & Biochemistry Program in the College of Engineering & Science at University of Detroit Mercy invites candidates to apply for a full-time chemistry lecturer position starting August 16, 2027. University of Detroit Mercy is committed to fostering a supportive and inclusive academic community and to advancing experiential and community-engaged learning. Our strong student outcomes led to recognition by The Wall Street Journal Best Colleges report, ranking Detroit Mercy 2 nd in Michigan and 36 th nationally. As a primarily undergraduate institution (PUI), Detroit Mercy offers small classes and opportunities for close collegial relationships. Faculty in the College of Engineering & Science form a dynamic community of teaching-scholars with a strong commitment to student-centered instruction and academic mentoring. The Chemistry & Biochemistry Program at Detroit Mercy is a vibrant program whose faculty teach courses required for students majoring in science and engineering discipline and courses within the university’s core curriculum. Faculty also engage in interdisciplinary and collaborative teaching and research and mentor students within the College of Engineering and Science. Chemistry & Biochemistry faculty have opportunities to collaborate in other disciplines and at partner institutions and organizations. We are particularly interested in candidates who can demonstrate through their teaching, experience, and service their ability to contribute to the Mission of the University and our commitment to provide support and opportunities for a diverse group of students across all disciplines. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong interest in applying evidence-based teaching and assessment practices. We seek an enthusiastic teacher-scholar who is committed to supporting students with a wide range of backgrounds and experiences and who can inspire and educate future scientists and engineers. Candidates must hold, at minimum, a master’s degree in chemistry or a chemistry-related discipline. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Teaching responsibilities will primarily consist of organic chemistry laboratory courses, which represent the position’s most significant instructional need. Depending on departmental needs, the successful candidate may also teach organic chemistry lectures and general chemistry lecture or laboratory courses. The typical teaching load for this lecturer position is four course sections per semester. Candidates must meet all required qualifications to be eligible for appointment. Preferred qualifications will be used to assess candidates’ preparation and fit for the position. Requirements Minimum Qualifications An earned master’s degree or higher in chemistry or a chemistry-related discipline. Experience teaching chemistry courses at the college level or other relevant instructional experience Demonstrated knowledge of evidence-based pedagogical practices that support student learning Demonstrated commitment to inclusive and equitable practices that support the mission and core values of the College of Engineering & Science . Preferred Qualifications Postdoctoral training (or other relevant experience). Commitment and ability to innovative, evidence-based teaching strategies that enhance student learning outcomes for a diverse undergraduate student body. Commitment to service of the department, college, university, and community in alignment with the mission of the university. Commitment to student-centered mentoring and advising a students’ holistic development, including encouraging students to reflect and engage with biology/science in a broader social context. Knowledge of the needs of students transitioning to university learning environment. Experience working with undergraduate students in the laboratory. Physical Requirements Job may require occasional lifting of light-weight objects (1 to 15 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Work Environment The position involves work in classroom, office, and chemistry laboratory environments. Laboratory work may involve the use of chemicals, scientific instruments, personal protective equipment, and established safety procedures. Salary/Pay Information Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Instructions to Applicants Candidates must complete an online application and upload all required materials: Cover letter: A detailed letter explaining how the candidate’s background and experience address the required and preferred qualifications. Curriculum vitae: A complete curriculum vitae that includes all instructional experience, with the course or activity title, the candidate’s role, and a brief description of responsibilities. Teaching statement: A statement of teaching experience and philosophy (maximum of two pages) that specifically addresses student-centered, evidence-based teaching and assessment practices. The statement should explain how these practices support the learning and holistic development of students with varied backgrounds and experiences. Mission statement: A statement (maximum of two pages) describing the candidate’s knowledge, experience, and plans for supporting the university’s mission and its values of mercy, justice, and compassion. The statement should also explain how the candidate plans to contribute through teaching and service to the university’s collegial and academic community. Professional references: Names and contact information for three professional references. Do not submit letters of recommendation with the initial application; letters will be requested for finalists. For full consideration, applications must be received by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on November 30, 2026 . Applications received after that date may be reviewed until the position is filled. Questions about the qualifications, required application materials, or search process may be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Kendra Evans, at evanskr@udmercy.edu . As Michigan's largest, most comprehensive private University, the University of Detroit Mercy is an independent Catholic institution of higher education sponsored by the Sisters of Mercy and Society of Jesus. Detroit Mercy seeks qualified candidates who will contribute to the University's mission, diversity, and excellence of its academic community. The University of Detroit Mercy is an Equal Opportunity Affirmative Action Employer with a diverse student body and welcomes persons of all backgrounds."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/udmercycareers/cx/job-details?reqId=5001225954006": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant. Position Classification FT Admin Position Summary The administrative assistant for the law career services office supports the student/graduate-centered and outcome-focused work of the career services team and provides administrative support to the office’s directors. This position is eligible for a hybrid work arrangement in accordance with applicable University policies. Essential Duties and Responsibilities 1. Daily Operations, Administrative, & Communications Serve as front-line CSO professional and support day-to-day operations Manage office phone, email, and calendar through cso@udmercy.edu account Assist with budget, expense reports, and processing accounts payable Manage subscriptions, including NALP, Crain’s, Legal News, MLW Maintain employer contact lists for engagement efforts Assist with CSO website and social media Assist with creation and proofreading of office publications Ensure communications are branded appropriately Manage office supplies and refreshments 2. Career Services Management (csm) Software Serve as main administrator for career services management software Ensure students and graduates are entered and coded correctly in system Support any data imports/migrations Assist with externship and clinical applications through career services management software 3. Job Postings Accept, investigate, post, and approve job postings Communicate postings to counselors and assist with disseminating to students and recent graduates Work directly with employers to maintain employment listings Administer reciprocity program and create content for BYU Intercollegiate Job Bank monthly newsletter. 4. Programs & Hosting Employers Support program planning and logistics Attend CSO programming and represent office at other law school programs Assist with invitations, scheduling, and execution of on-campus interview and other employer programs 5. Data Collection, Research, & Records Maintain CSO files and records Assist with collecting and reporting graduate employment outcomes and demographics Assist with tracking student employment outcomes, including 1L outcomes, OCI outcomes, and clerkship outcomes 6. Resources & Relationships Develop and maintain relationships with students, alumni, and employers through prompt and excellent service Maintain relationships with internal colleagues to ensure smooth cross-departmental collaboration. 5% Other Duties as Assigned Minimum Qualifications Education – A High School Diploma (HR Confirmed). Employment – Two to five years of experience (HR Confirmed). Preferred Qualifications A college degree or work experience. High attention to detail required. Superior communication skills required. Grammar and organizational skills required. Must possess a professional appearance. Must possess a service attitude. Must possess the ability to multi-task in a distracting environment and meet deadlines. Must be self-motivated and innovative. Ability to maintain confidentiality required. Knowledge of legal education and the legal profession helpful, but not required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Technology skills required. Proficiency with Office products, including, but not limited to, Word, PowerPoint, Outlook, and Excel. Physical Requirements Job may require lifting light weight objects (1 to 10 pounds) with no repetitive bending or stooping. Occasionally lift average weight objects (1 to 10 pounds). Work Environment Regular exposure to favorable conditions such as those found in a normal office. Salary/Pay Information Commensurate with experience Anticipated Schedule 8:30 AM to 5:00 PM Hybrid work schedule to be determined with the team to ensure coverage of the office."
    }
  },
